  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 723.05 Non-Central Treatment Implementation Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 723.05 Non-Central Treatment Implementation Requirements.\n\n(a) The requirements of this section shall apply after a PWS owner receives approval for the installation and use of non-central treatment devices pursuant to Env-Dw 723.02 and Env-Dw 723.03 and complies with Env-Dw 723.04.\n\n(b) With respect to the contract required by Env-Dw 723.02(i), the PWS owner shall:\n\n(1) Not allow the contract to lapse for greater than 15 days; and\n\n(2) Make the contract available for review by department staff upon request.\n\n(c) With respect to the non-central treatment devices installed, the owner shall:\n\n(1) Operate and maintain each non-central treatment device, including those installed in private homes or businesses, as specified in the monitoring plan approved under Env-Dw 723.04, by maintaining a contract with a certified operator for specific implementation of operation and maintenance;\n\n(2) Submit data documenting that every building and every device within such building is subject to treatment and monitoring; and\n\n(3) Not separate the non-central treatment device from the PWS by sale, lease, or other conveyance of the property.\n\n(d) Monitoring shall be in accordance with Env-Dw 723.08.\n\nSource. #10618, eff 6-1-14, EXPIRED 6-1-24\n\nNew. #14119, eff 11-23-24, EXPIRES: 11-23-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
